From: B Honey <9922368+Mhsbrian@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 20:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] OPENBOOK: TerminalApp: the agent bridge says which image is
 installed

A Linux environment the Terminal app installed before OpenBook's pinned
image (patch 0003) is Google's, which has no quired. The bridge called
it running like any other, so Quire waited for a quired that would
never answer and could not say why.

call("status"), call("start") and call("stop") now also return image,
the first line of the installed image's build_id, whenever one is
installed: openbook_x86_64-... for OpenBook's, ferrochrome/x86_64/
hourly-... for Google's. It is read on every call, since Recovery can
replace the image while the app runs, and capped at 200 characters.

OpenBook ANAL-394 (Quire setup: a Linux environment without Quire's
helper).

Change-Id: I3f2b6a0d94c1e7b85a2d6c0f4e9b1a7d3c5e8f20
---
 .../terminal/AgentBridgeProvider.kt           | 25 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 24 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

